### **5. SceneGeometry Data Interface**
📍 [elements/ui/index.tsx](elements/ui/index.tsx#L17931)

Defines the data structure for 3D objects:
```tsx
export interface SceneGeometry {
  guid: string;
  plane?: Plane;
  isSelected?: boolean;
  isHovered?: boolean;
  isFocusable?: boolean;
  onClick?: () => void;
  onPointerEnter?: () => void;
  onPointerLeave?: () => void;
}
```

---

### **6. No BVH Implementation Found**
- No `BVH` or bounding-volume-hierarchy setup detected
- Raycasting uses standard THREE.js raycaster with default settings
- Performance optimized via `frameloop="demand"` (render-on-demand)

**Summary:** The Scene component uses a standard react-three/fiber Canvas with demand-based rendering and pointer-based raycasting. The Geometry component provides visual feedback through colors and emissive materials for hover/select states. Raycasting is enabled via standard THREE.Mesh raycast assignment, with no specialized BVH optimization.

